Project: TasteHub — Modern Food Delivery Website

Act as a senior UI/UX designer, full-stack developer, software architect, and e-commerce specialist. Build a complete, modern, premium food delivery website called TasteHub, using the uploaded reference image as the primary design inspiration.

The website must look polished, professional, visually rich, user-friendly, and production-ready. Do not create just a static landing page or a simple UI mockup. Build a complete food ordering platform with functional frontend interactions, backend APIs, database integration, authentication, cart management, checkout, order tracking, and an admin dashboard.

Use the reference image to reproduce its overall visual identity: dark food photography hero, orange accents, white content sections, circular food category icons, featured food cards, promotional banners, customer reviews, app promotion, and dark footer.

1. Technology stack

Use the following technologies where supported by the development environment:

Frontend: React with Next.js and TypeScript.
Styling: Tailwind CSS with reusable design components.
UI components: shadcn/ui or an equivalent accessible component library.
Icons: Lucide React.
Animations: Framer Motion or lightweight CSS animations.
Backend: Next.js server actions/API routes or a separate Node.js backend.
Database: PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM, or Supabase.
Authentication: Supabase Auth or secure session-based authentication.
Image storage: Supabase Storage or another suitable image hosting service.
Payments: Stripe or an appropriate payment gateway for the deployment country, with support for Razorpay where applicable in India.
Maps and location: Google Maps or a suitable geolocation/maps provider.
Deployment: Vercel or another compatible hosting platform.

Choose a consistent stack and implement it fully rather than mixing unnecessary technologies. If a service requires credentials, create clearly documented environment variables and provide a functional development fallback without exposing secrets.

